# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots MariaDB (holding the weak phpass wp_users password
# hashes) and apache, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the DB is ALREADY running for verify.sh to query the live credential store;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting the DB cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Note: password hashes are data read on every query, so re-hashing them takes
# effect WITHOUT a restart - there is no "forgot to restart" variant. Preserving
# the CMD ensures the check reads the live database and a dead DB is a FAILURE.
